  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows high volatility (spikes >5%) and sentiment is neutral or slightly positive; true outcomes often reverse direction immediately after the first forecast step.",
    "When sentiment shifts from negative to positive (e.g., -1.00 to 1.00) within the last 3 days, the model fails to capture the subsequent mean reversion or crash, instead projecting a slow linear uptrend.",
    "Model forecasts consistently overshoot by 4-8 EUR in the first 5 days following a period of consolidation (price range <2 EUR); true outcomes frequently drop below the historical average during these phases.",
    "In high-volatility regimes, the model's 30-day horizon is systematically biased toward the recent local maximum rather than the long-term trend, ignoring the 'mean reversion' signal present in the sentiment history.",
    "When sentiment remains flat (0.00) for >5 days while price fluctuates within a tight band, the model should apply a downward correction factor of 3-5% to its forecasted trajectory."
  ]
}
